1. Informational: User seeking knowledge (e.g. 'what is execution definition language');
2. Navigational: User seeking a specific site/page (e.g. 'chatr login');
3. Commercial Investigation: User evaluating options before purchase (e.g. 'chatr vs microsoft teams enterprise review');
4. Transactional: User ready to execute or purchase (e.g. 'buy talentxcel recruitment pack').

1. LCP (Largest Contentful Paint): Measures perceived loading speed. Good threshold: <= 2.5 seconds;
2. INP (Interaction to Next Paint): Measures page responsiveness and UI delay. Good threshold: <= 200 milliseconds;
3. CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift): Measures visual stability during load. Good threshold: <= 0.1.

- 301 Moved Permanently: Transfers 90%+ link equity to the new target URL;
- 302 Found (Temporary): Tells crawlers to retain the original URL in the index;
- 404 Not Found: Page missing; crawlers deindex after multiple failed passes;
- 410 Gone: Explicit signal that the page was intentionally removed, accelerating immediate deindexing.

